  "scope": "The actual 1800-slot caller first scans original cost fields and constructs the retained adjacency matrix, then hands that literal returned matrix and original endpoint pointers into the real zero-row/context/shortest machine. All child transitions and returns share one append-only heap. The exact result fields match original constant-zero shortest on keptAdjacency with the original zeroMask. The input-only bound includes terminal physical charge. Eight physical cases check literal paths or absence, including removed/retained interior vertices and padding. Original graph/cost/vertex representations, valid endpoints, address widths and the later ordered avoiding-demand scan/outer dispatch remain explicit.",
